    "q-181990": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181990",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $B=\\{9,\\,3,\\,0,\\,7\\}?$\n\n$min(B)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,max(B)=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(B) & =min\\{9,\\,3,\\,0,\\,7\\}=0 \\\\ max(B) & =max\\{9,\\,3,\\,0,\\,7\\}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
