    "q-182028": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182028",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set ${R}_{0}^{+}?$\n\nThe set has no {{field-1}}, while the {{field-2}} is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition, ${R}_{0}^{+}=[0,\\infty ).$\n\nThis set has $\\text{no maximum},$ while \n\n$$\nmin({R}_{0}^{+})=min[0,\\infty )=0.\n$$",
